{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "label": "JetStream KV + Object Store", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstreamkeyvalueactor", "label": "JetStreamKeyValueActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A separate actor from JetStreamActor because a bucket is not a stream + consumer; folding them together would have given the stream actor a sixth mode nobody wants. target is required where an answer is the point (get, keys, watch) and optional where it is a receipt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstreamobjectstoreactor", "label": "JetStreamObjectStoreActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_compare_and_swap", "label": "KV compare-and-swap via revision", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "revision is the concurrency token: write back with expectedRevision and the server rejects the write if anyone moved the key in between, answering keyValueOperationFailed so the caller retries against the fresh value. expectedRevision:0 means 'only if the key does not exist yet'.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_watch", "label": "KV watch change feed", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A watch is desired state, not a one-shot subscription: re-established on every reconnect, and one issued while disconnected lands on the next connect. It matters more here than elsewhere because a change feed that silently stops looks exactly like a bucket that stopped changing.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_create_false_bind", "label": "create:false binds an existing bucket", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "With create:false the actor binds to an existing bucket and fails the connect if it is missing \u2014 the right setting when an operator provisions the bucket and a typo should not quietly produce an empty one.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_maxobjectbytes", "label": "Whole-object ceiling (maxObjectBytes)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An object body rides the BrokerActor outbound buffer, which is bounded in MESSAGES (1000) not bytes and evicts the oldest on overflow \u2014 so a multi-megabyte body means up to outboundBuffer x body resident while disconnected and an overflow silently discards an upload. v1 therefore caps bodies at maxObjectBytes (1 MiB): a put over the cap is refused before the body enters the buffer, a get over the cap is refused from metadata before the body is fetched.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_operation_failure_not_disconnect", "label": "A failed operation does not drop the connection", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A per-key or per-object failure is reported to target as keyValueOperationFailed / objectStoreOperationFailed. Only 'not connected' throws, because throwing out of the dispatch path is how the base class learns the transport died \u2014 one rejected key is not that.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstreamkeyvalueactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstreamobjectstoreactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_compare_and_swap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_watch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_create_false_bind", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/jetstream-kv.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_jetstream_kv", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_jetstream_kv_maxobjectbytes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "E